## Lore

The Ojahee come from a Mega-Damage world rich in magic energy, where their
nation was in the middle of its own industrial revolution: black-powder rifles
that would pass for cannons in human hands, steam trains and airships, and new
factories. They were a rising warrior power, well on the way to conquering
their neighbors, when the Dakir snatched one of their best regiments out of a
jungle campaign.

Under the slavers the regiment learned to fight in loose skirmish lines
instead of massed volleys and axe-bayonet charges, but it remains a force of
shock troops. In heavy armor behind personal force fields, carrying plasma
rifles that hit like tank guns, an Ojahee trooper can trade blows with
armored vehicles.

Ojahee prize courage, invention and honor, and the Legion''s Ojahee are more
warlike still than their kin at home. They regard humans as clever, childlike
"little cousins", which makes for deep friendships at best and condescension
at worst.
', 'published', 'data-script'
WHERE NOT EXISTS (SELECT 1 FROM imported_classes WHERE class_id = 'ojahee');


-- Read the result back rather than trusting the exit code. d1-apply prints
-- these, and a CR in the stored markdown means the checkout mangled the file.
SELECT class_id, name, status, length(markdown) AS bytes, instr(markdown, char(13)) > 0 AS has_cr
  FROM imported_classes WHERE class_id = 'ojahee';

